Hi all,

Please help me improve Next3 user experience by answering this short
survey and/or forwarding it to anyone who may be interested in trying
out Next3 snapshots.

I've made some improvements to the Next3 file system, which will make
the upcoming release 1.0.12 accessible to more users:
- Next3 can be built as a stand-alone kernel module and does not
require to patch/build a kernel.
- Next3 module was ported to several stable kernels
(2.6.{29.3,31.11,32.12}) and could be easily ported to other kernel
versions per request.

1. Did you try to use Next3 snapshots?

2. Would you try to use Next3 snapshots if it didn't require building
a new kernel?

3. Would you be interested in a port for a kernel version not
specified on the list above?

4. Other comments about improving user experience or how to reach a
wider group of users?

Thanks for your time,
Amir.
